<%# A production's next date on Ticketing home (Tim, 2026-10-16: the rows were
    cluttered): its wide image (or the name's two letters), when, what, how
    it's selling, its sales status only when that's news, and Work the door
    while that show's door is open. From sm up: the picture, the title over
    its time, how it's selling and the button beside them. On a phone: the
    picture down the left, when over the title, the sold count on the right,
    and Work the door full width under all of it (Tim, 2026-11-08: squeezed
    in beside the title it cut the title to two words). "Online sales
    closed" is never said here (Tim, same day: useless on this row).
    Locals: listing, stats. %>
<%
  starts = listing.show.date_and_time
  when_words = starts.to_date == Date.current ? "Tonight · #{starts.strftime('%-l:%M %p')}" : starts.strftime("%a, %b %-d · %-l:%M %p")
  label, badge_classes = ticket_listing_status_badge(listing, stats.inventory)
  door_open = DoorTonight.door_open?(listing)
  # A mini bar under the sold words (Tim, 2026-10-16), the same math as the
  # drawer's date lines, on every screen size (Tim liked it on desktop and
  # wanted it on his phone too).
  seats = stats.seats_to_sell
  percent = seats.to_i.positive? ? [ (stats.sold_anywhere * 100.0 / seats).round, 100 ].min : (seats&.zero? ? 100 : nil)
%>
<%# On a phone the grid places these by column and row: the picture and the
    sold count span the two lines of words between them, and the button
    takes a row of its own under everything. %>
<div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 sm:px-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] gap-x-3 gap-y-0.5 items-center sm:flex sm:gap-4">
  <div class="row-span-2 sm:row-span-1">
    <%= render "shared/wide_thumb", image: listing.show.wide_image_for_rows, name: listing.display_title, width: "w-16 sm:w-24" %>
  </div>
  <div class="contents sm:block sm:flex-1 sm:min-w-0">
    <span class="col-start-2 row-start-1 block text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap"><%= when_words %></span>
    <%= link_to listing.display_title, manage_ticket_listing_path(listing), class: "col-start-2 row-start-2 block min-w-0 text-sm sm:text-[15px] font-semibold text-gray-900 truncate hover:text-pink-700" %>
  </div>
  <span class="col-start-3 row-start-1 row-span-2 sm:row-span-1 text-right text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">
    <%= stats.sold_words %>
    <% if percent %>
      <span class="block mt-1 ml-auto h-1.5 w-16 sm:w-24 rounded-full bg-gray-100" title="<%= percent %>% sold"><span class="block h-1.5 rounded-full bg-pink-500" style="width: <%= percent %>%"></span></span>
    <% end %>
    <% unless label.in?([ "On sale", "Online sales closed" ]) %><span class="block mt-1 text-xs font-medium <%= badge_classes[/text-\S+/] %>"><%= label %></span><% end %>
  </span>
  <% if door_open %>
    <div class="col-span-3 row-start-3 mt-2.5 sm:mt-0 sm:flex-shrink-0" data-coming-up-door>
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Work the door", variant: "primary", size: "small", classes: "w-full sm:w-auto max-sm:py-2.5", path: door_path(listing) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
